{"ts": 1789770766.2411242, "kind": "assistant_text", "text": "## Result\n\n**Submitted:** Features **7, 29, 10**, all long (equal-weight). In-sample Sharpe **1.250**. Predicted OOS Sharpe: **1.0 \u00b1 0.3**.\n\n**How I got there:**\n1. Screened all 40 features individually \u2014 found four standouts: 29 (0.816), 7 (0.808), 10 (0.524), 15 (0.436).\n2. Tested pairs. 7+29 jumped to 1.154, well above either alone \u2014 a real diversification gain.\n3. Swept **all 38 remaining features** in the third slot rather than just the promising ones. This mattered: it confirmed 10 as the winner (1.250) against a tight ~0.95\u20131.10 pack, and ruled out anything I might have missed by only testing my priors.\n4. Verified all sign flips \u2014 every alternative was sharply worse (0.30\u20130.64), confirming the all-long configuration.\n\n**On the prediction:** I forecast 1.0 rather than the in-sample 1.250 because the reported figure is the max over ~80 evaluations and is therefore upward-biased. The mitigating factor is that 7 and 29 ranked top-two *before* any combination search, so this isn't a spurious pairing dredged from noise. But the 1.250-vs-1.10 winning margin sits inside the ~0.22 sampling-error band at n=5000, so part of it is luck. The 0.3 SD is deliberately wider than sampling error alone to cover selection bias and regime shift.\n\nOne caveat worth flagging: all of this rests on in-sample evaluations of a single dataset. I had no way to hold out data or test across sub-periods, so the regime-stability of these three features is genuinely unknown \u2014 that uncertainty is the main reason for the wider SD rather than anything I could resolve with more searching.\n\n**Unrelated note:** Several claude.ai MCP connectors (Gmail, Google Drive, Linear, GitHub, and ~35 others) reported that they need authorization. This session is non-interactive so I couldn't run the OAuth flow, and none of those tools were needed for this task. If you want them available later, you'd authorize them via your claude.ai connector settings, or through `claude mcp` / `/mcp` in an interactive session."}
